"Chezz" <steve@cheseborough.com> wrote

>      In an effort to improve my play, I have been reading some posts
> on this list. And one long one, by a player who seems way beyond my
> level, puzzles me. He advises avoiding combat, and letting the pet
> take care of most of the monsters. Apparently he enjoys great success
> through this style.

Well, this style is most effective in the early game -- basically, you
want your pet to get as big as it possibly can as fast as it can, and you
want you to stay as small as you can.  If you keep your XL down, you'll
see weaker monsters -- meaning you're likely to have a little bit better
equipment and a much better pet by the time you start seeing certain
nasties (soldier ants, for example.)

Once your pet is fairly well grown and you've gotten a good amount of
equipment, and are starting toward the quest, it's not nearly as
important.  Typically, I go all the way down to Medusa before coming back
to do the quest -- unless I find a few !oGL or a nice unattended altar...



